</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.4.3 </span>Evaluation on ImageNet-ESC</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to our vision-language experiments, we perform few-shot evaluation using the 5-fold splits defined in the benchmark. Each fold contains 8 samples per class, with one fold used for training and validation and the remaining four for testing. We repeat the process over 5 random splits and report the average performance. For audio encoding, we use AudioCLIP with an ES-ResNeXT backbone <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guzhov et al., 2021</a>]</cite>. AudioCLIP is pretrained on AudioSet and generates audio embeddings in the same representation space as CLIP. Following the instructions in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guzhov et al., 2021</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2023</a>]</cite>, we use <span id="A2.SS4.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">train()</span> mode in Pytorch to extract the features since <span id="A2.SS4.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">eval()</span> mode yields suboptimal embeddings. We evaluate our models on two tasks—audio classification and image classification—comparing the unimodal baseline against two multimodal variants in which the primary modality is each time augmented by one of the other modalities.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.4.4 </span>Transfer Learning from Language to Vision</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To adapt a language model to image classification, we embed image patches using a linear projection and add positional encodings to capture spatial structure. We then use transformer layers initialized from pretrained BERT, and finally, a 2-layer MLP classification head. Specifically, we split each image of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224\times 224" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>224</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>224</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224\times 224</annotation></semantics></math> into patches of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\times 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\times 16</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="196" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>196</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">196</annotation></semantics></math> patch tokens. Each patch is then projected into the model’s embedding space of dimension <math id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d(e.g.\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(e.g.\ </annotation></semantics></math>d=768 for GPT-2, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1024</annotation></semantics></math> for BERT) via a learned linear layer. We then prepend a learnable “<span id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[CLS]</span>” token, add learned positional embeddings of shape <math id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N+1)\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N+1)\times d</annotation></semantics></math>, and apply dropout with probability <math id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>. This <math id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N+1)\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N+1)\times d</annotation></semantics></math> sequence is passed into the pretrained transformer stack (either GPT-2 or BERT), using a full bidirectional attention mask over all patch tokens and the CLS token. We extract the final hidden state corresponding to the CLS token and feed it through a two-layer MLP classification head.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">During training, we evaluate two scenarios: 1) one where the pretrained backbone is frozen and only the patch embedding and linear head are trained, and 2) another where the backbone is initially frozen to align the trainable layers (patch embedding and head) with the pretrained language backbone, and then unfrozen after 2000 steps for end-to-end training. This approach allows us to test whether the semantic richness captured by language models provides a strong initialization, leading to better convergence and performance compared to training ViT from scratch.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs of Theoretical Results</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present complete derivations and proofs of the main theoretical claims. <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Background and Definitions ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> gathers all definitions and background required for our arguments. <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Maximum Likelihood Estimators and Fisher Contributions ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> formalizes the linear data‐generating model, derives closed-form maximum-likelihood estimators for each modality and their joint estimator, and computes the corresponding block-wise Fisher information. Finally, <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Theorems and Proofs ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> provides the detailed proofs of our variance-reduction claims, showing rigorously how unpaired multimodal estimation strictly lowers estimator variance.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Background and Definitions</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we revisit the mathematical definitions used in our theoretical analysis, including matrix‐orderings, characterization of symmetric matrices and Fisher information.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Positive Semidefinite Matrix)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A real symmetric matrix <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">positive semidefinite</em> if for all vectors <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}A\,v\;\geq\;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}A\,v\;\geq\;0.</annotation></semantics></math> Equivalently, all eigenvalues of <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> are nonnegative. We denote the set of all <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> symmetric, positive-semidefinite matrices as <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{d}_{\succeq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{d}_{\succeq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Positive Definite Matrix)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A real symmetric matrix <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">positive definite</em> if for every nonzero <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}A\,v\;&gt;\;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}A\,v\;&gt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math> Equivalently, all eigenvalues of <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly positive. We denote the set of all <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> symmetric, positive definite matrices as <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{d}_{\succ 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{d}_{\succ 0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Loewner Order)<span id="Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For two real symmetric matrices <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\preceq B\;\Longleftrightarrow\;B-A\text{ is positive semidefinite}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is positive semidefinite</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\preceq B\;\Longleftrightarrow\;B-A\text{ is positive semidefinite}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\prec B\;\Longleftrightarrow\;B-A\text{ is positive definite}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≺</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is positive definite</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\prec B\;\Longleftrightarrow\;B-A\text{ is positive definite}</annotation></semantics></math>. This defines a partial order on the cone of symmetric matrices.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fisher Information Matrix)<span id="Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a parametric family of densities <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> on data <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Fisher information matrix</em> at parameter <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p(\cdot;\theta)}\!\bigl[\nabla_{\theta}\log p(x;\theta)\,\nabla_{\theta}\log p(x;\theta)^{\top}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p(\cdot;\theta)}\!\bigl[\nabla_{\theta}\log p(x;\theta)\,\nabla_{\theta}\log p(x;\theta)^{\top}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, for regular models,
<math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\;I(\theta)=-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\nabla^{2}_{\theta}\log p(x;\theta)\bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\;I(\theta)=-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\nabla^{2}_{\theta}\log p(x;\theta)\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Maximum Likelihood Estimators and Fisher Contributions</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we revisit our linear data–generating model, introduce notations for the <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>–only, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>–only and joint likelihoods, derive the closed‐form MLEs <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{X,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{X,Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and formalize their information contributions towards estimating the ground truth parameters <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\equiv[\theta_{c},\theta_{x},\theta_{y}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\equiv[\theta_{c},\theta_{x},\theta_{y}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data Generating Process.</span> Recall our linear data-generating process: Assume that all factors of variation in reality live in a single <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional space <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{*}\equiv\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≡</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{*}\equiv\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> modeled using a linear data-generating pipeline. This parameter can further be decomposed as <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\equiv[\theta_{c},\theta_{x},\theta_{y}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\equiv[\theta_{c},\theta_{x},\theta_{y}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{c}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}},\theta_{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}},\theta_{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{c}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}},\theta_{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}},\theta_{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{c}+d_{x}+d_{y}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{c}+d_{x}+d_{y}=d</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> captures the <em id="A3.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">common</em> (shared) parameters that affect both modalities, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the parameters that only affect modality <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the parameters that only affect modality <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>. We observe two independent datasets, one from each modality <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N_{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N_{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Y_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Y_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, each reflecting partial measurements of the ground truth latent space <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{i}\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{i}\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;A_{c,i}\,\theta_{c}\;+\;A_{x,i}\,\theta_{x}\;+\;\epsilon_{X,i},\quad\epsilon_{X,i}\sim\mathcal{N}\bigl(0,\,\sigma_{x}^{2}I_{m_{i}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;A_{c,i}\,\theta_{c}\;+\;A_{x,i}\,\theta_{x}\;+\;\epsilon_{X,i},\quad\epsilon_{X,i}\sim\mathcal{N}\bigl(0,\,\sigma_{x}^{2}I_{m_{i}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{j}\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{j}\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;B_{c,j}\,\theta_{c}\;+\;B_{y,j}\,\theta_{y}\;+\;\epsilon_{Y,j},\quad\epsilon_{Y,j}\sim\mathcal{N}\bigl(0,\,\sigma_{y}^{2}I_{n_{j}}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;B_{c,j}\,\theta_{c}\;+\;B_{y,j}\,\theta_{y}\;+\;\epsilon_{Y,j},\quad\epsilon_{Y,j}\sim\mathcal{N}\bigl(0,\,\sigma_{y}^{2}I_{n_{j}}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{c,i},A_{x,i},B_{c,j},B_{y,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{c,i},A_{x,i},B_{c,j},B_{y,j}</annotation></semantics></math> are known design blocks capturing how each sample probes the latent factors and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{X,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{X,i}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="A3.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{Y,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{Y,j}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the independent measurement noise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In our linear setting, estimating the true latent state <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>—and hence the underlying reality <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>—is governed by the Fisher information matrix <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta)\;=\;-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\nabla^{2}_{\theta}\,\ell(\theta)\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta)\;=\;-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\nabla^{2}_{\theta}\,\ell(\theta)\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math>, which measures how sharply the likelihood “curves” around the true <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. High curvature along a particular axis means the data tightly constrain that component, driving down estimator variance there.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unimodal Estimators.</span> We first estimate <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> using only the <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>–dataset. Stacking <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields a design matrix <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> with block rows <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A_{c,i},\,A_{x,i},\,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A_{c,i},\,A_{x,i},\,0]</annotation></semantics></math>. The least-squares solution</p>
<table id="A3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{X}=\arg\min_{\theta}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}\bigl\lVert X_{i}-A_{c,i}\,\theta_{c}-A_{x,i}\,\theta_{x}\bigr\rVert^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{X}=\arg\min_{\theta}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}\bigl\lVert X_{i}-A_{c,i}\,\theta_{c}-A_{x,i}\,\theta_{x}\bigr\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">omits <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> entirely. Consequently, the Fisher information on <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes, making it unidentifiable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Analogously, stacking <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Y_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Y_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> defines <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> with block rows <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[B_{c,j},\,0,\,B_{y,j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[B_{c,j},\,0,\,B_{y,j}]</annotation></semantics></math> and yields</p>
<table id="A3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{Y}=\arg\min_{\theta}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\bigl\lVert Y_{j}-B_{c,j}\,\theta_{c}-B_{y,j}\,\theta_{y}\bigr\rVert^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{Y}=\arg\min_{\theta}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\bigl\lVert Y_{j}-B_{c,j}\,\theta_{c}-B_{y,j}\,\theta_{y}\bigr\rVert^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This estimator doesn’t depend on <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, providing zero coverage for that component. Thus, each unimodal estimator entirely fails to recover the parameters exclusive to the omitted modality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multimodal Estimators.</span> Despite the lack of one-to-one pairing, both <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Y_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Y_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math> share the common parameters <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the two distributions are conditionally independent, the joint likelihood factorizes as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=1}^{N_{x}}p(X_{i}\mid\theta_{c},\theta_{x})\;\times\;\prod_{j=1}^{N_{y}}p(Y_{j}\mid\theta_{c},\theta_{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">×</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=1}^{N_{x}}p(X_{i}\mid\theta_{c},\theta_{x})\;\times\;\prod_{j=1}^{N_{y}}p(Y_{j}\mid\theta_{c},\theta_{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Maximizing this yields the combined estimator</p>
<table id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{X,Y}=\arg\min_{\theta_{c},\theta_{x},\theta_{y}}\biggl\{\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}\|X_{i}-A_{c,i}\,\theta_{c}-A_{x,i}\,\theta_{x}\|^{2}\;+\;\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\|Y_{j}-B_{c,j}\,\theta_{c}-B_{y,j}\,\theta_{y}\|^{2}\biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{X,Y}=\arg\min_{\theta_{c},\theta_{x},\theta_{y}}\biggl\{\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}\|X_{i}-A_{c,i}\,\theta_{c}-A_{x,i}\,\theta_{x}\|^{2}\;+\;\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\|Y_{j}-B_{c,j}\,\theta_{c}-B_{y,j}\,\theta_{y}\|^{2}\biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, there is no requirement to match up individual <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{i},Y_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{i},Y_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> pairs. Instead, the estimate for <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is improved by both modalities while remaining unpaired.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fisher Information.</span> In our linear model, each dataset contributes block‐structured Fisher information. For the <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>–dataset:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{X}=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}\begin{pmatrix}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}&amp;A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{x,i}&amp;0\\
A_{x,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}&amp;A_{x,i}^{\top}A_{x,i}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{X}=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}\begin{pmatrix}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}&amp;A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{x,i}&amp;0\\
A_{x,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}&amp;A_{x,i}^{\top}A_{x,i}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">and for the <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>–dataset:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{Y}=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\begin{pmatrix}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}&amp;0&amp;B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{y,j}\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\\
B_{y,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}&amp;0&amp;B_{y,j}^{\top}B_{y,j}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{Y}=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\begin{pmatrix}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}&amp;0&amp;B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{y,j}\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\\
B_{y,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}&amp;0&amp;B_{y,j}^{\top}B_{y,j}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> samples are independent, their curvature contributions add pointwise, resulting in the joint Fisher information being simply the sum of the unimodal blocks.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{X,Y}=I_{X}+I_{Y}=\begin{pmatrix}\sum_{i}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}+\sum_{j}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}&amp;*&amp;*\\
*&amp;\sum_{i}A_{x,i}^{\top}A_{x,i}&amp;0\\
*&amp;0&amp;\sum_{j}B_{y,j}^{\top}B_{y,j}\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{X,Y}=I_{X}+I_{Y}=\begin{pmatrix}\sum_{i}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}+\sum_{j}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}&amp;*&amp;*\\
*&amp;\sum_{i}A_{x,i}^{\top}A_{x,i}&amp;0\\
*&amp;0&amp;\sum_{j}B_{y,j}^{\top}B_{y,j}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p">where “<math id="A3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math>” denotes the cross‐modal blocks. In particular, we have the shared‐parameter block as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}+\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}+\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Theorems and Proofs</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The aim of this section is to detail the proofs of the theoretical results presented in the main manuscript
The key theoretical tools driving our analysis are already prepared in <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Background and Definitions ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> and  <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Maximum Likelihood Estimators and Fisher Contributions ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>. Core to our theoretical analysis are a few lemmas around the Loewner‐order monotonicity result for inverses that we prove below.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Loewner Order reversal for inverses)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,N\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,N\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\prec N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≺</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\prec N</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\preceq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\preceq N</annotation></semantics></math>). Then <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{-1}\prec M^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≺</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{-1}\prec M^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{-1}\preceq M^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{-1}\preceq M^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>) .</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> exists and is nonsingular.
Define <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=N^{-1/2}MN^{-1/2}\prec I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≺</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=N^{-1/2}MN^{-1/2}\prec I</annotation></semantics></math>. Because a congruence with an invertible matrix preserves positive-definiteness, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>; hence <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is well defined and <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{-1}\succ I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≻</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{-1}\succ I</annotation></semantics></math> (the scalar map <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto x^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto x^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly decreasing on <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>).
Undoing the congruence gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M^{-1}=N^{-1/2}C^{-1}N^{-1/2}\succ N^{-1/2}IN^{-1/2}=N^{-1}.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≻</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>I</mi><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-1}=N^{-1/2}C^{-1}N^{-1/2}\succ N^{-1/2}IN^{-1/2}=N^{-1}.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Inverse–monotonicity of the Moore–Penrose pseudoinverse)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,N\in\mathbb{S}_{\succeq 0}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,N\in\mathbb{S}_{\succeq 0}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\prec N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≺</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\prec N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ker M=\ker N=\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ker M=\ker N=\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}K</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then their pseudoinverses obey <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\dagger}\prec M^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>≺</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\dagger}\prec M^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=K^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=K^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=P_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=P_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be the orthogonal projector onto <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> vanish on <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the decompositions
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=PMP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=PMP</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=PNP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=PNP</annotation></semantics></math>.
Restricted to <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> both matrices are positive–definite:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{M}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=PMP,\qquad\tilde{N}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=PNP\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}^{\dim S},\quad\tilde{M}\prec\tilde{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≺</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=PMP,\qquad\tilde{N}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=PNP\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}^{\dim S},\quad\tilde{M}\prec\tilde{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Loewner Order reversal for inverses). ‣ C.3 Theorems and Proofs ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{M},\tilde{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M},\tilde{N}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain
<math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{N}^{-1}\prec\tilde{M}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≺</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{N}^{-1}\prec\tilde{M}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Moore–Penrose pseudoinverse equals the ordinary inverse on <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and is
zero on <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\dagger}=P\tilde{M}^{-1}P,\qquad N^{\dagger}=P\tilde{N}^{-1}P." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\dagger}=P\tilde{M}^{-1}P,\qquad N^{\dagger}=P\tilde{N}^{-1}P.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore
<math id="A3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\dagger}=P\tilde{N}^{-1}P\prec P\tilde{M}^{-1}P=M^{\dagger}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>≺</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\dagger}=P\tilde{N}^{-1}P\prec P\tilde{M}^{-1}P=M^{\dagger}.</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Directional Loewner Order reversal)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,N\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,N\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\preceq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\preceq N</annotation></semantics></math>.
If a non-zero vector <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}Mv&lt;v^{\!\top}Nv," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}Mv&lt;v^{\!\top}Nv,</annotation></semantics></math>
then</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the vector </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, it holds that </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}M^{-1}v\geq v^{\!\top}N^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}M^{-1}v\geq v^{\!\top}N^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, with strict inequality </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}M^{-1}v&gt;v^{\!\top}N^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}M^{-1}v&gt;v^{\!\top}N^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and only if </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N-M)M^{-1}v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N-M)M^{-1}v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a non-zero vector </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\!\top}M^{-1}u&gt;u^{\!\top}N^{-1}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\!\top}M^{-1}u&gt;u^{\!\top}N^{-1}u</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote the Loewner gap
<math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=N-M\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=N-M\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the assumption <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}Nv&gt;v^{\!\top}Mv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}Nv&gt;v^{\!\top}Mv</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}\Delta v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}\Delta v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Introduce the congruence–invariant normalisation <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=M^{-1/2}\Delta M^{-1/2}\succeq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=M^{-1/2}\Delta M^{-1/2}\succeq 0.</annotation></semantics></math>
Now, using <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=M^{1/2}CM^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=M^{1/2}CM^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> and properties of inverse,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N\;=\;M^{1/2}(I+C)M^{1/2},\qquad N^{-1}\;=\;M^{-1/2}(I+C)^{-1}M^{-1/2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\;=\;M^{1/2}(I+C)M^{1/2},\qquad N^{-1}\;=\;M^{-1/2}(I+C)^{-1}M^{-1/2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+C\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+C\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> (because <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex16X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M^{-1}-N^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M^{-1}-N^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=M^{-1/2}\!\Bigl[I-(I+C)^{-1}\Bigr]M^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=M^{-1/2}\!\Bigl[I-(I+C)^{-1}\Bigr]M^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex16Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=M^{-1/2}C(I+C)^{-1}M^{-1/2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=M^{-1/2}C(I+C)^{-1}M^{-1/2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-(I+C)^{-1})(I+C)=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-(I+C)^{-1})(I+C)=C</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, evaluating in the direction <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex17X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v^{\!\top}(M^{-1}-N^{-1})v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v^{\!\top}(M^{-1}-N^{-1})v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=v^{\!\top}M^{-1/2}(I+C)^{-1}CM^{-1/2}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=v^{\!\top}M^{-1/2}(I+C)^{-1}CM^{-1/2}v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex17Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u^{\!\top}(I+C)^{-1}Cu\quad(\text{where }u=M^{-1/2}v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>where </mtext><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u^{\!\top}(I+C)^{-1}Cu\quad(\text{where }u=M^{-1/2}v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now, since <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I+C)^{-1}\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I+C)^{-1}\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{S}_{\succeq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{S}_{\succeq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> commute, the matrix <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I+C)^{-1}C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I+C)^{-1}C</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite and it has exactly the same kernel as <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, if <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=Q\operatorname{diag}(\lambda_{i})Q^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=Q\operatorname{diag}(\lambda_{i})Q^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A3.SS3.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\geq 0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\geq 0)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}C(I+C)^{-1}u=\sum_{i}\frac{\lambda_{i}}{1+\lambda_{i}}\,(Q^{\top}u)_{i}^{2}\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}C(I+C)^{-1}u=\sum_{i}\frac{\lambda_{i}}{1+\lambda_{i}}\,(Q^{\top}u)_{i}^{2}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">This expression is strictly positive exactly when <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> has a component in any eigen-subspace with <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> i.e when <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\not\in\mathrm{ker}(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\not\in\mathrm{ker}(C)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M^{-1/2}\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-1/2}\in\mathbb{S}_{\succ 0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Cu=0\implies M^{-1/2}\Delta M^{-1/2}u=0\implies\Delta M^{-1}v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cu=0\implies M^{-1/2}\Delta M^{-1/2}u=0\implies\Delta M^{-1}v=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, this expression is strictly positive if <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta M^{-1}v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta M^{-1}v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, from the premise <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}\Delta v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}\Delta v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible, <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is also not the zero matrix. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, this means that <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> must have at least one strictly positive eigenvalue. Let <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be such an eigenvalue, and let <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> be a corresponding eigenvector. Define, <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=M^{1/2}z\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=M^{1/2}z\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\!\top}(M^{-1}-N^{-1})x=z^{\!\top}C(I+C)^{-1}z=\frac{\lambda}{1+\lambda}\|z\|^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\!\top}(M^{-1}-N^{-1})x=z^{\!\top}C(I+C)^{-1}z=\frac{\lambda}{1+\lambda}\|z\|^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, showing the existence of a non-zero vector <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\!\top}M^{-1}x&gt;x^{\!\top}N^{-1}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\!\top}M^{-1}x&gt;x^{\!\top}N^{-1}x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheoremx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheoremx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem </span><a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Variance Reduction with Unpaired Multimodal Data). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span><span id="Thmtheoremx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Variance Reduction with Unpaired Multimodal Data). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)<span id="Thmtheoremx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheoremx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{X},\hat{\theta}_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{X},\hat{\theta}_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the least-squares estimators for <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>
using only <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and only <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Y_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Y_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the joint estimator using both unpaired datasets. Then, under the assumption that at least one <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{c,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{c,j}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,2,...N_{y}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,2,...N_{y}\}</annotation></semantics></math> has full rank, the common-factor covariance satisfies the strict Loewner ordering i.e. <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\prec\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}},\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≺</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\prec\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}},\quad</annotation></semantics></math>
or equivalently, the Fisher information on <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> strictly increases when combining both modalities, despite not having sample-wise pairing: <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{X}+I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\succ(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{X}+I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\succ(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any statistic <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(\theta)=\nabla_{\theta}\log p(x;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(\theta)=\nabla_{\theta}\log p(x;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and vector <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}I(\theta)\,v=v^{\top}\mathbb{E}[S(\theta)S(\theta)^{\top}]\,v=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(v^{\top}S(\theta))^{2}\bigr]\;\geq\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}I(\theta)\,v=v^{\top}\mathbb{E}[S(\theta)S(\theta)^{\top}]\,v=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(v^{\top}S(\theta))^{2}\bigr]\;\geq\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, a Fisher Information Matrix is a positive semidefinite matrix.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">In our linear–Gaussian model, the <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>–dataset contributes <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{x}}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>–dataset gives <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since at least one <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{c,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{c,j}</annotation></semantics></math> has full column rank, <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive‐definite on the <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> subspace. Now, if at least one <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{c,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{c,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> has full column rank <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}\,v=\|B_{c,j}v\|^{2}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}\,v=\|B_{c,j}v\|^{2}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, each summand in <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite and at least one is positive definite, so their sum <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite on the <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> subspace. Thus,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\;\prec\;(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}+(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=(I_{X}+I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≺</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\;\prec\;(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}+(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=(I_{X}+I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, for regular exponential families (including Gaussian linear models), the covariance matrix of the
maximum likelihood estimator <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> near the true <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is (asymptotically) the inverse of the Fisher information matrix i.e. <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{\theta})\;\approx\;I(\theta_{0})^{-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{\theta})\;\approx\;I(\theta_{0})^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math> Precisely, as the sample size <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}(\hat{\theta}-\theta_{0})\overset{d}{\to}\mathcal{N}(0,I(\theta_{0})^{-1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}(\hat{\theta}-\theta_{0})\overset{d}{\to}\mathcal{N}(0,I(\theta_{0})^{-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the true parameter value, <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is the Fisher Information Matrix evaluated at <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,I(\theta_{0})^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,I(\theta_{0})^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a multivariate normal distribution with mean <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance matrix <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta_{0})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta_{0})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we compare variances via the Moore–Penrose pseudoinverse of the information matrices.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X,Y}=(I_{X}+I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X,Y}=(I_{X}+I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X,Y}=M_{X}+M_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X,Y}=M_{X}+M_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is also positive definite (as <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X,Y}\succeq M_{Y}\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⪰</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X,Y}\succeq M_{Y}\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus, <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})=M_{X,Y}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})=M_{X,Y}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have established <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}\prec M_{X,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>≺</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}\prec M_{X,Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite (to define the matrix <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>), we apply <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Loewner Order reversal for inverses). ‣ C.3 Theorems and Proofs ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to get
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X,Y}^{-1}\prec M_{X}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>≺</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X,Y}^{-1}\prec M_{X}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\;=\;M_{X,Y}^{-1}\;\prec\;M_{X}^{-1}=\mathrm{Var}\!\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">≺</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\;=\;M_{X,Y}^{-1}\;\prec\;M_{X}^{-1}=\mathrm{Var}\!\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the statement under the condition that <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite. Note here that, on spaces unidentifiable by <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-alone i.e. <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{ker}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{ker}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X,Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite, it has finite variance along such <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> i.e. <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, thus strictly reducing the variance of the estimator. Thus, adding the unpaired <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>-modality strictly reduces the variance (or, dually,
increases the Fisher information) on the common factors <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1x1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem1">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1x1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem </span><a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Directional Variance Reduction with Unpaired Multimodal Data). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span><span id="Thmtheorem1x1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Directional Variance Reduction with Unpaired Multimodal Data). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)<span id="Thmtheorem1x1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let all notation be as in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Variance Reduction with Unpaired Multimodal Data). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and define <math id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{XY}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=M_{X}+M_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{XY}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=M_{X}+M_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If there exists at least one index <math id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,2,...N_{y}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,2,...N_{y}\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem1x1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{c,j}v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{c,j}v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then the following hold:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1x1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Fisher information strictly increases in direction </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> i.e. </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M_{XY}\,v&gt;v^{\top}M_{X}v." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M_{XY}\,v&gt;v^{\top}M_{X}v.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The variance of the estimator in direction </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is strictly reduced i.e </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\,\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&lt;v^{\top}\,\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\,\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&lt;v^{\top}\,\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v,</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\not\in\mathrm{range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\not\in\mathrm{range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. For </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, this strict inequality holds for </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> under an additional invertibility condition and is always guaranteed for some </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathrm{range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathrm{range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> i.e. </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists u</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> s.t. </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}\,\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,u&lt;u^{\top}\,\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}\,\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,u&lt;u^{\top}\,\mathrm{Var}\bigl(\hat{\theta}_{X}\bigr)_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,u</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{X}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}},\;M_{Y}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}},\;andM_{XY}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=M_{X}+M_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}},\;M_{Y}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}},\;andM_{XY}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=M_{X}+M_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. By assumption, <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists j</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{c,j}v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{c,j}v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M_{Y}v=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\|B_{c,j}v\|^{2}\geq\|B_{c,j}v\|^{2}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M_{Y}v=\sum_{j=1}^{N_{y}}\|B_{c,j}v\|^{2}\geq\|B_{c,j}v\|^{2}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive-definite in direction <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, implying <math id="A3.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X,Y}\succ M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X,Y}\succ M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> in this direction:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M_{XY}v=v^{\top}M_{X}v+v^{\top}M_{Y}v&gt;v^{\top}M_{X}v," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M_{XY}v=v^{\top}M_{X}v+v^{\top}M_{Y}v&gt;v^{\top}M_{X}v,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">thus proving the first part of the theorem.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1: <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> If <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has a non-zero component in <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ker}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ker}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=v_{S}+v_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=v_{S}+v_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{S}\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{S}\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}\in\mathrm{ker}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}\in\mathrm{ker}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The linear combination of parameters <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\theta_{c}=v_{S}^{\top}\theta_{c}+v_{K}^{\top}\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\theta_{c}=v_{S}^{\top}\theta_{c}+v_{K}^{\top}\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}\in\mathrm{ker}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}\in\mathrm{ker}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>, the component <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}^{\top}\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}^{\top}\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is not identifiable by the <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-only model.
Consequently, the asymptotic variance of an unbiased estimator for <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\theta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\theta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> using only the <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-dataset is infinite. We denote this as
<math id="A3.SS3.p15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">The strict inequality <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M_{XY}v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M_{XY}v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, ensures that <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin\mathrm{ker}(M_{XY})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin\mathrm{ker}(M_{XY})</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{XY})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{XY})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{XY})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{XY})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{XY}^{\dagger}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{XY}^{\dagger}v</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined. Furthermore, because <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{XY}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{XY}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite, <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{XY}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{XY}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> is also positive semidefinite and shares the same kernel as <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{XY}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{XY}</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{XY}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{XY}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric). As <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin\mathrm{ker}(M_{XY})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin\mathrm{ker}(M_{XY})</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin\mathrm{ker}(M_{XY}^{\dagger})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin\mathrm{ker}(M_{XY}^{\dagger})</annotation></semantics></math>, which ensures <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M_{XY}^{\dagger}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M_{XY}^{\dagger}v</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite positive value.
Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Comparing this to the variance from the <math id="A3.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-only model in this case:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v&lt;\infty=v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v&lt;\infty=v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">and the strict inequality holds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2: <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Let <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be the orthogonal projector
onto <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}=M_{X}P_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}=M_{X}P_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{XY}=M_{X}+M_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{XY}=M_{X}+M_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, the restrictions</p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{M}_{X}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=P_{S}M_{X}P_{S},\qquad\tilde{M}_{XY}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=P_{S}M_{XY}P_{S}=\tilde{M}_{X}+P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Y</mi></msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}_{X}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=P_{S}M_{X}P_{S},\qquad\tilde{M}_{XY}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=P_{S}M_{XY}P_{S}=\tilde{M}_{X}+P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p18.2" class="ltx_p">are <em id="A3.SS3.p18.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">positive-definite</em> on <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>; To see this, take any non-zero <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in S</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\mathrm{range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\mathrm{range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S}w=w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S}w=w</annotation></semantics></math>; hence</p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}w=w^{\top}M_{X}w\;&gt;\;0\quad\text{($P_{S}$ is identity when restricted to $S$)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mtext> is identity when restricted to </mtext><mi>S</mi><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}w=w^{\top}M_{X}w\;&gt;\;0\quad\text{($P_{S}$ is identity when restricted to $S$)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p18.3" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{M}_{X}\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}_{X}\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="A3.SS3.p18.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
adding it preserves positive-definiteness, so</p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{M}_{XY}=\tilde{M}_{X}+P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}\succeq\tilde{M}_{X}\;\succ\;0\quad\text{on }S." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}_{XY}=\tilde{M}_{X}+P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}\succeq\tilde{M}_{X}\;\succ\;0\quad\text{on }S.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Directional Loewner Order reversal). ‣ C.3 Theorems and Proofs ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(1) to <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{M}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{M}_{XY}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}_{XY}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> gives us <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{XY}^{-1}v\leq v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{XY}^{-1}v\leq v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math>. Strict inequality <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{XY}^{-1}v&lt;v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{XY}^{-1}v&lt;v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math> holds if and only if the condition <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=((\tilde{M}_{XY}-\tilde{M}_{X})\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}v\neq\mathbf{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=((\tilde{M}_{XY}-\tilde{M}_{X})\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}v\neq\mathbf{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is met. Therefore, if condition <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> holds, the directional variance along this constrained space <math id="A3.SS3.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly reduced:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{XY}^{-1}v&lt;v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}v=v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{XY}^{-1}v&lt;v^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}v=v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Further, from <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Directional Loewner Order reversal). ‣ C.3 Theorems and Proofs ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(2), there exists some non-zero vector <math id="A3.SS3.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in S</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS3.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}\tilde{M}_{XY}^{-1}u&lt;u^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}\tilde{M}_{XY}^{-1}u&lt;u^{\top}\tilde{M}_{X}^{-1}u</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus we have,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}u&lt;u^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}u." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}u&lt;u^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, completing the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume a direction <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=v^{\top}(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=v^{\top}(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=v^{\top}(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=v^{\top}(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is the common eigenvector of <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the variance in direction <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> contracts by the factor</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})\,v}{v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})\,v}\;=\;\frac{1/(a+b)}{1/a}\;=\;\frac{a}{a+b}\;&lt;\;1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})\,v}{v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})\,v}\;=\;\frac{1/(a+b)}{1/a}\;=\;\frac{a}{a+b}\;&lt;\;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">So the joint estimator achieves strictly lower error along <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By assumption, <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is a common eigenvector of <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}v=\lambda_{X}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}v=\lambda_{X}v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}v=\lambda_{Y}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}v=\lambda_{Y}v</annotation></semantics></math>
for some eigenvalues <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. From the assumptions, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{X}=a/\|v\|^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{X}=a/\|v\|^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{Y}=b/\|v\|^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{Y}=b/\|v\|^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric and <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}v=\lambda_{X}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}v=\lambda_{X}v</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{X}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{X}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the pseudoinverse acts as <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}^{\dagger}v=\lambda_{X}^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}^{\dagger}v=\lambda_{X}^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the variance in direction <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for the <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-only estimator is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v=v^{\top}M_{X}^{\dagger}v=v^{\top}(\lambda_{X}^{-1}v)=\lambda_{X}^{-1}\|v\|^{2}=a^{-1}\|v\|^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v=v^{\top}M_{X}^{\dagger}v=v^{\top}(\lambda_{X}^{-1}v)=\lambda_{X}^{-1}\|v\|^{2}=a^{-1}\|v\|^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p22.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p22.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is a common eigenvector, it is also an eigenvector of <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{XY}=M_{X}+M_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{XY}=M_{X}+M_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{X}+M_{Y})v=M_{X}v+M_{Y}v=\lambda_{X}v+\lambda_{Y}v=(\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y})v." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{X}+M_{Y})v=M_{X}v+M_{Y}v=\lambda_{X}v+\lambda_{Y}v=(\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y})v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p22.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p22.3.1" class="ltx_text">The corresponding eigenvalue is <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{XY}=\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{XY}=\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{X}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{X}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{Y}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{Y}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{XY}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{XY}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{X}+M_{Y})^{\dagger}v=(\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y})^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{X}+M_{Y})^{\dagger}v=(\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y})^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math>.
The variance in direction <math id="A3.SS3.p22.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for the joint estimator is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v=v^{\top}(M_{X}+M_{Y})^{\dagger}v=(\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y})^{-1}\|v\|^{2}=(a+b)^{-1}\|v\|^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v=v^{\top}(M_{X}+M_{Y})^{\dagger}v=(\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y})^{-1}\|v\|^{2}=(a+b)^{-1}\|v\|^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p22.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p22.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we form the ratio of these variances:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v}{v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v}=\frac{\lambda_{X}}{\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y}}=\frac{a}{a+b}&lt;1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v}{v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v}=\frac{\lambda_{X}}{\lambda_{X}+\lambda_{Y}}=\frac{a}{a+b}&lt;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p22.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p22.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 2</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume a direction <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})\,v\;=\;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})\,v\;=\;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})\,v\;&lt;\;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})\,v\;&lt;\;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>
i.e. a direction unidentifiable from <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> alone becomes well‐posed with even unpaired data from <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">This corollary follows directly from Case 1 of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Directional Variance Reduction with Unpaired Multimodal Data). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The condition <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{ker}((I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{ker}((I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\not\in\mathrm{range}((I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\not\in\mathrm{range}((I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the additional condition <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the conclusions of Case 1 of the theorem apply directly.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance Reduction for Eigenvectors of <math id="Thmcorollary3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmcorollary3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> be an eigenvector of <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> with a corresponding eigenvalue <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{X}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{X}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. If the <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>-dataset provides information in this direction <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M_{Y}v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M_{Y}v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>), then the variance in direction <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly reduced by incorporating the <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>-dataset:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&lt;v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&lt;v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcorollary3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Specifically, <math id="Thmcorollary3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=\lambda_{X}^{-1}\|v\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=\lambda_{X}^{-1}\|v\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.9" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}=(I_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{Y}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{Y}=(I_{Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenvector of <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> with a positive eigenvalue <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{X}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{X}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\mathrm{Range}(M_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The variance using only the <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-dataset in direction <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=v^{\top}M_{X}^{\dagger}v." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=v^{\top}M_{X}^{\dagger}v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p24.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p24.2.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenvector of <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{X}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{X}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}^{\dagger}v=\lambda_{X}^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}^{\dagger}v=\lambda_{X}^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=v^{\top}(\lambda_{X}^{-1}v)=\lambda_{X}^{-1}\|v\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v=v^{\top}(\lambda_{X}^{-1}v)=\lambda_{X}^{-1}\|v\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p24.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p24.3.1" class="ltx_text">This scenario falls under Case 2 of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Directional Variance Reduction with Unpaired Multimodal Data). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, specifically its conclusion regarding <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in S</annotation></semantics></math>. According to that theorem, strict variance reduction <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v&lt;v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v&lt;v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}v</annotation></semantics></math> occurs if the condition <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}=((P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S})(M_{X}|_{S})^{-1}v\neq\mathbf{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}=((P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S})(M_{X}|_{S})^{-1}v\neq\mathbf{0})</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Here, <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal projector onto <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}|_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}|_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.SS3.p24.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{X}|_{S})^{-1}v=\lambda_{X}^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{X}|_{S})^{-1}v=\lambda_{X}^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">The condition <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> thus becomes <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S})(\lambda_{X}^{-1}v)\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S})(\lambda_{X}^{-1}v)\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{X}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{X}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, this is equivalent to <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}v\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}v\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We are given that <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M_{Y}v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M_{Y}v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S}v=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S}v=v</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M_{Y}v=v^{\top}P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M_{Y}v=v^{\top}P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{S}=P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{S}=P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> restricted to <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive semidefinite operator on <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. The condition <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}A_{S}v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}A_{S}v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in S,v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in S,v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{S}v\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{S}v\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (because if <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{S}v=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{S}v=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}A_{S}v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}A_{S}v=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which contradicts <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}A_{S}v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}A_{S}v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>).
Thus, <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}v\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S}M_{Y}P_{S}v\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means the condition <math id="A3.SS3.p25.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfied.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in S</annotation></semantics></math> and the condition <math id="A3.SS3.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> for strict inequality is met, by <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Directional Variance Reduction with Unpaired Multimodal Data). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, it follows that
<math id="A3.SS3.p26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&lt;v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X,Y})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v&lt;v^{\top}\mathrm{Var}(\hat{\theta}_{X})_{\theta_{c},\theta_{c}}\,v.</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3x1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem3">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3x1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem </span><a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Data from Auxiliary Modality Can Outperform More of the Same). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span><span id="Thmtheorem3x1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Data from Auxiliary Modality Can Outperform More of the Same). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical Perspectives ‣ 3 Unpaired Multimodal Representation Learning ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)<span id="Thmtheorem3x1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define for any <math id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{X}^{(m)}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{X}^{(m)}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}A_{c,i}^{\top}A_{c,i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{Y}^{(m)}=\sum_{j=1}^{m}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{Y}^{(m)}=\sum_{j=1}^{m}B_{c,j}^{\top}B_{c,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{range}\bigl(I_{Y}^{(m)}\bigr)\;\not\subseteq\;\mathrm{range}\bigl(I_{X}^{(m)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">⊈</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{range}\bigl(I_{Y}^{(m)}\bigr)\;\not\subseteq\;\mathrm{range}\bigl(I_{X}^{(m)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists a nonzero <math id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem3x1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}I_{Y}^{(m)}\,v&gt;v^{\top}I_{X}^{(m)}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}I_{Y}^{(m)}\,v&gt;v^{\top}I_{X}^{(m)}v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.10" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{X}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\operatorname{range}\!\bigl(I_{X}^{(m)}\bigr),\;R_{Y}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\operatorname{range}\!\bigl(I_{Y}^{(m)}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:2.416em;" width="2.416em"><mi>range</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:2.416em;" width="2.416em"><mi>range</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{X}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\operatorname{range}\!\bigl(I_{X}^{(m)}\bigr),\;R_{Y}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}=\operatorname{range}\!\bigl(I_{Y}^{(m)}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math>
By the assumption <math id="A3.SS3.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{Y}\not\subseteq R_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>⊈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{Y}\not\subseteq R_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose a vector
<math id="A3.SS3.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in R_{Y}\setminus R_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in R_{Y}\setminus R_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite dimensional inner product space and <math id="A3.SS3.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is its finite dimensional subspace, we can decompose <math id="A3.SS3.p27.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=w_{||}+v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">⁣</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=w_{||}+v</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A3.SS3.p27.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{||}\in R_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">⁣</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{||}\in R_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p27.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in R_{X}^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in R_{X}^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="A3.SS3.p27.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\notin R_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\notin R_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, the orthogonal component <math id="A3.SS3.p27.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS3.p28.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i) Term from <math id="A3.SS3.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{X}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{X}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A3.SS3.p28.1.2" class="ltx_text">
From the </span><span id="A3.SS3.p28.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fundamental Theorem of Linear Algebra</span><span id="A3.SS3.p28.1.4" class="ltx_text">, for any symmetric matrix <math id="A3.SS3.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ker S=\operatorname{range}(S)^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ker S=\operatorname{range}(S)^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>;
hence <math id="A3.SS3.p28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{X}^{\perp}=\ker I_{X}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{X}^{\perp}=\ker I_{X}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}I_{X}^{(m)}v=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}I_{X}^{(m)}v=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS3.p29.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii) Term from <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{Y}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{Y}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A3.SS3.p29.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Because <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in R_{Y}=\operatorname{range}(I_{Y}^{(m)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in R_{Y}=\operatorname{range}(I_{Y}^{(m)})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A3.SS3.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=I_{Y}^{(m)}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=I_{Y}^{(m)}u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose, for contradiction, that <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{Y}^{(m)}v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{Y}^{(m)}v=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\ker I_{Y}^{(m)}=R_{Y}^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>Y</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\ker I_{Y}^{(m)}=R_{Y}^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\perp w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\perp w</annotation></semantics></math>.
But
<math id="A3.SS3.p29.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\cdot v=(w_{\parallel}+v)\cdot v=w_{\parallel}\!\cdot v+\|v\|^{2}=\|v\|^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>∥</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>∥</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\cdot v=(w_{\parallel}+v)\cdot v=w_{\parallel}\!\cdot v+\|v\|^{2}=\|v\|^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
because <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\perp w_{\parallel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>∥</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\perp w_{\parallel}</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This contradicts <math id="A3.SS3.p29.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\perp w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\perp w</annotation></semantics></math>; therefore
<math id="A3.SS3.p29.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{Y}^{(m)}v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{Y}^{(m)}v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and, by positive semidefiniteness,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}I_{Y}^{(m)}v&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}I_{Y}^{(m)}v&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the above inequalities yields
<math id="A3.SS3.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\!\top}I_{Y}^{(m)}v&gt;v^{\!\top}I_{X}^{(m)}v," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\!\top}I_{Y}^{(m)}v&gt;v^{\!\top}I_{X}^{(m)}v,</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A3.SS3.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the desired inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>UML: Algorithm Pseudocode</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we present the full pseudocode for <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Uml</span> for both the self-supervised and supervised settings as shown in <a href="#alg1" title="In Appendix D UML: Algorithm Pseudocode ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and  <a href="#alg2" title="In Appendix D UML: Algorithm Pseudocode ‣ Better Together: Leveraging Unpaired Multimodal Data for Stronger Unimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> respectively.</p>
</div>
